WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.800
Glitches have always been a part of video
games.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.380
It's kind of a modern miracle that today's
games, as ridiculously complex as they are,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.860
don't bug out constantly.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.459
A few pixels out of place is one thing, but
the realism of today's games can produce bugs

00:00:15.459 --> 00:00:19.890
that run the gamut from weird and quirky to
scream-your-face-off scary.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.240
Take, for instance, Assassin's Creed Unity!

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.160
But that's just the beginning.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.460
Here are some of the most bizarre visual glitches
you'll find today.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.960
MLB The Show 17: The Wicker Man

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.400
Like many ultra-customizable games, MLB The
Show 17 allows you to create baseball players

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.280
from the ground up.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:44.240
Its interface uses sliders to let gamers adjust
their virtual-ballplayers' features.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.760
Want a dude with an Amish beard, Steve Buscemi's
come-hither eyes, and crippling male pattern

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:50.260
baldness?

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.800
That sexy dream is within your grasp.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.010
While most glitches are usually discovered
by players, it was Sony themselves who revealed

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.480
that this very slider system can glitch out.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.180
The unaltered results?

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.640
A nightmarish, Lovecraftian horror.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Behold!

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.340
"Ahhhh!"

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.780
So if you want a baseball player whose head
essentially becomes a skull-shaped bundle

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.740
of dry spaghetti, it's all yours.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.900
You want human eyes crying sadly from within
a nest of ground beef?

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.600
Well, isn't that really what baseball is all
about?

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:21.760
"Are you crying?

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.240
Are you crying?!

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.200
There's no crying.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.120
There's no crying in baseball!"

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.960
Sony San Diego's Twitch streams leading up
to the game's release unveiled the glitch,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.280
and said that it was something the team has
been "working on."

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.180
It's a bit unclear if this means that they're
working on fixing it, or if they decided to

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.860
make MLB The Show a survival horror series
without telling anyone.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:46.520
The Sims 4: Demon babies

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:52.200
As far as reality simulators go, The Sims
series is a little more realistic than, say,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.000
Goat Simulator.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.220
And it's great if you're really into….

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.580
Bathroom design?

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.640
But it still has its share of surreal moments,
and many of them come in the form of babies.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.280
Terrifying, horrible monster babies.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:10.020
Sure, the birth of a baby is usually a joyous
occasion for your Sim, but in The Sims 4,

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.920
you may just want to kill it with fire.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.720
One little glitch and your bundle of joy can
come out deformed in ways that no actual human

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:22.690
could ever survive: eyeballs stuck to the
end of antennae, or twisted, misshapen bodies

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:24.880
that kinda just make you want to barf forever.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.020
Yes, the developers came along with a patch
fixed the glitch, but the internet never forgets.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.240
Overwatch: The vanishing oasis

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:39.320
The Oasis map in Overwatch has a distinct,
futuristic-art-deco meets Middle Eastern style.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.500
It forces players to deal with traffic hazards,
in addition to the usual hail of lasers and

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.000
bullets.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:48.220
It's a brilliant design, as long as it sticks
around.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.780
Which it doesn't always do.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.620
The Oasis map glitch can give players an existential
crisis.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.520
Repeatedly jumping in a certain spot causes
the ground to completely disappear.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.820
Cars plummet into the abyss, and your character
is left hanging in endless space as the game's

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.180
physics go out the window.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:08.640
Fortunately, if you just wait it out long
enough, you'll die.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:09.560
Easy fix.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.440
Donkey Kong Country: Tropical Freeze: Secret
Swimming

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.810
If you're one of the millions of gamers who
passed on the Wii U, you missed the most punishingly

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.320
difficult entry in the entire Donkey Kong
Country series: Tropical Freeze.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.770
You'll probably be killed hundreds of times,
but you also won't be able to stop playing.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:33.240
The game's water levels are among its most
brutal, but a glitch in Shipwreck Shore allows

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.150
you to pretty much bypass the whole thing,
allowing you to access a weird, watery, parallel

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.760
universe underneath the level, where the surface
world sometimes appears upside down.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:48.000
Swimming along in the Upside Down is the strangest
watery weirdness since Super Mario's minus

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:48.500
world.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.440
Fallout 4: Insane horrors

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:56.280
It sold truckloads of copies, earned rave
reviews, and won a ton of awards.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.680
But no one's going to deny that Fallout 4
is also incredibly buggy.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.540
And when it glitches out, it goes all in.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.470
The game is creepy enough as is, but the accidental
faceless horrors that the game produces defy

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.120
anything that designers could have come up
with on purpose.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.570
One glitch causes animals to merge with objects
and start multiplying while hovering demonically

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.220
in the air.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:23.320
Another can cause your character's death animation
to spiral wildly out of control, sending your

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.220
floppy corpse pirouetting hundreds of feet
in the air.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.840
Of course, while game publisher Bethesda has
done its best to patch all of these bugs out

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.600
of existence, they've all been logged for
posterity.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.800
Because the future needs to remember that
horrible, deformed mutants are people too.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.180
Red Dead Redemption: Manimals

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.500
Another excellent game plagued by bugs, Red
Dead Redemption had some notorious animal

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.640
problems — and they weren't the kind an
exterminator could fix.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:54.160
Not only could your trusty horse basically
become a rocket sled, but animal avatars occasionally

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.380
got mixed up with humans.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.400
And the results were not pretty.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.940
Players could famously encounter a woman whose
head was mashed up with that of a donkey...

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.380
who you could then hop on and ride around.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:10.260
The same glitch could also spawn roaming cougar-men,
elk-horses, and flying bird people.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.100
"Hahaha!"

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:17.080
Sometimes, the game would even let a human
ride another, or a horse briefly ride its

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.080
human, which is illegal in 42 states.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.900
We're not saying Red Dead Redemption 2 should
exclusively feature human-riding horses…

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.680
except it totally should.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.520
Grand Theft Auto V: Drowning in paperwork

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:33.960
Rockstar's hugely popular Grand Theft Auto
series isn't without its share of memorable

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:34.460
glitches, either.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:38.180
And Grand Theft Auto V kept the tradition
alive admirably.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.500
One glitch in particular may just make you
want to quit your day job.

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.380
If you spawn as Michael on the film set, you'll
be standing next to a guy holding a clipboard.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.620
Startle him, and another clipboard will pop
out of nowhere.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:55.740
If you happen to be using, say, an especially
terrifying gun, this can result in a rapid

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.830
and ongoing series of startles, and a fountain
of clipboards, which begin piling up around

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.760
the hapless man.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:06.280
Keep at this long enough, and the guy will
fall screaming into this pool of clipboards

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.080
and vanish.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:07.960
Forever.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.760
Which is only slightly more horrific than
working in a real office.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.200
Madden 15: Tiny titan

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:20.200
Gamers who love imaginary football eagerly
await the latest edition of Madden every year,

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.820
and rookies can't wait to see how they're
represented by the beloved franchise.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:29.170
But when it came to middle linebacker Christian
Kirksey, Madden 15 may have gotten his physical

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:31.280
stats just a little bit wrong.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:37.560
Kirksey, drafted by the Browns in 2014, is
listed in the game at 1 foot, 2 inches tall

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.320
and 235 pounds.

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.260
"This, we didn't make this up, this is real.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.389
Here he is, in action, in the video game.

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:44.700
Lot of people talking about this.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:48.520
There he… hey guys!"

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.060
It's as much of a disadvantage as you would
think.

00:06:51.540 --> 00:06:55.860
While he has no trouble keeping up with opposing
players, his tackling leaves a little to be

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.540
desired.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.000
But he can handle the ball just fine…so
long as it's really close to the ground.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.600
The real Kirksey had a great sense of humor
about the whole thing, tweeting that he found

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.760
it "hilarious" and taking the opportunity
to offer words of encouragement.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.120
"No matter how small, have big dreams and
live big!"

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.080
Thanks for watching!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.870
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.620
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

